  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Show that each of the following functions is a bijection:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f:\\mathbb{Z}\\to\\mathbb{Z}$ where $f(n)=-n$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Bijective: injective and surjective.\n\nEqual outputs give equal inputs; every integer $m$ has preimage $-m$.",
          "worked": "Injectivity. If $f(n)=f(m)$, then\n$$\\begin{align*}-n&=-m\\\\n&=m.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $f$ is injective.\n\nSurjectivity. For any $m\\in\\mathbb{Z}$, choose $n=-m\\in\\mathbb{Z}$. Then\n$$f(-m)=-(-m)=m.$$\nThus $f$ is surjective, so $f$ is a bijection.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f:[0,1]\\to[0,2]$ where $f(x)=2x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Bijective: injective and surjective.\n\nEqual outputs give equal inputs; every $y\\in[0,2]$ has preimage $\\frac{y}{2}\\in[0,1]$.",
          "worked": "Injectivity. If $f(u)=f(v)$, then\n$$\\begin{align*}2u&=2v\\\\u&=v.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $f$ is injective.\n\nSurjectivity. For any $y\\in[0,2]$, solve\n$$\\begin{align*}2x&=y\\\\x&=\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $0\\le y\\le2$, we have $\\frac{y}{2}\\in[0,1]$, and\n$$f\\left(\\frac{y}{2}\\right)=2\\left(\\frac{y}{2}\\right)=y.$$\nThus $f$ is surjective, so $f$ is a bijection.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f:(0,\\infty)\\to(0,1)$ where $f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Bijective: injective and surjective.\n\nEqual outputs give equal inputs; every $y\\in(0,1)$ has positive preimage $\\frac{y}{(1-y)}$.",
          "worked": "Injectivity. If $f(u)=f(v)$, then\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{u}{u+1}&=\\frac{v}{v+1}\\\\\\frac{u+1-1}{u+1}&=\\frac{v+1-1}{v+1}\\\\1-\\frac{1}{u+1}&=1-\\frac{1}{v+1}\\\\\\frac{1}{u+1}&=\\frac{1}{v+1}\\\\u+1&=v+1\\\\u&=v.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $f$ is injective.\n\nSurjectivity. For any $y\\in(0,1)$, solve\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{x+1}&=y\\\\x&=yx+y\\\\x-yx&=y\\\\x&=\\frac{y}{1-y}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $0<y<1$, both $y$ and $1-y$ are positive, so $\\frac{y}{(1-y)}\\in(0,\\infty)$. Also,\n$$\\begin{align*}f\\left(\\frac{y}{1-y}\\right)&=\\frac{\\frac{y}{1-y}}{\\frac{y}{1-y}+1}\\\\f\\left(\\frac{y}{1-y}\\right)&=y.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $f$ is surjective, so $f$ is a bijection.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 125
      }
    ]
  },
